# m5stick-s3-pikud

ESPHome firmware + Home Assistant snippets for Pikud display on M5Stack Stick S3.

## Layout

- `esphome/` — flashable firmware (`m5stick-s3.yaml`); secrets in gitignored `secrets.yaml`
- `homeassistant/` — merge into HA config; see `homeassistant/README.md`
- `docs/` — architecture and troubleshooting

## Constraints

- Stick needs **2.4 GHz** Wi-Fi; ESPHome secrets stay out of git.
- Display driver state uses `sensor.m5stick_pikud_display_state`, not `sensor.oref_alert` directly.
- Live `ok` is idle; green SAFE only on real all-clear or `test_ok`.
- Test scripts bump `input_number.m5stick_pikud_sync` before changing mode.
- No double-click handling yet — single short + A long only.

## Changes

- Firmware + HA template changes usually ship together.
- Run `esphome config` / CI before pushing YAML edits.
- OTA target: `m5stick-s3.local` after first USB flash.
